{
  "name": "How to Research Questions for AI Content",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Identify Core Services and Topics",
      "text": "Start by breaking down your business services or product categories. Instead of broad categories, think about the specific problems or needs your services address. This helps narrow down your focus for question research.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: Utilize Google Search Console for Unanswered Questions",
      "text": "Dive into your Google Search Console. Look for queries where your site appeared but didn't get clicks, or for keywords related to your services that show high impressions but low click-through rates. These often highlight 'unanswered questions' where AI could fill a gap.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Explore Q&A Platforms and Forums",
      "text": "Spend time on platforms like Quora, Reddit, and specific industry forums (e.g., Avvo for legal, Houzz for home services, Yelp Q&A, Google Business Profile Q&A). What are people asking about your services or common issues they face? Pay attention to the exact phrasing people use.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Research Real-World Queries with Tools",
      "text": "Use tools like the Perplexity API (in deep research mode) or similar services. Look for specific, scenario-based questions people are asking, like \"emergency plumber near me\" or \"best way to care for hardwood floors.\" This helps identify high-intent, conversational queries.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: Prioritize Questions by Intent and Volume",
      "text": "Once you have a long list, prioritize them. Which questions are most frequently asked? Which indicate a strong intent to buy or use a service? Focusing on these will yield the most impactful AI-ready content. By systematically researching these questions, you build a foundation for content that isn't just keyword-stuffed, but genuinely useful and highly likely to be picked up by AI systems. Remember, the goal is to be the reliable source that provides clear, concise answers.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": [
